#. Tag: author
#: cosmicdist.docbook:3
#, no-c-format
msgid "<firstname>Akarsh</firstname> <surname>Simha</surname>"
msgstr "<firstname>Akarsh</firstname> <surname>Simha</surname>"

#. Tag: title
#: cosmicdist.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Cosmic Distance Ladder</title>"
msgstr "<title>Tabela kosmičkih udaljenosti</title>"

#. Tag: primary
#: cosmicdist.docbook:9
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>Cosmic Distance Ladder</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>Tabela kosmičkih udaljenosti</primary>"

#. Tag: para
#: cosmicdist.docbook:10
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The cosmic distance ladder refers to the succession of different methods "
"that astronomers use to measure distances to objects in the sky. Some "
"methods, like <link linkend=\"ai-parallax\">parallax</link>, work well for "
"only nearby objects. Other methods, like using the <firstterm>cosmological "
"redshift</firstterm>, work only for very distance galaxies. Thus, there are "
"several methods, each with its own limited validity, and hence the name."
msgstr ""
"Tabela kosmičkih udaljenosti odnosi se na uspjeh  različitih metoda koje "
"astronomi koriste za mjerenje udaljenosti objekata na nebu. Neke metode, kao "
"što su <link linkend=\"ai-parallax\">parallax</link>, dobro radi samo za "
"obližnje objekte. Druge metode, kao što su  <firstterm>kosmološki crveni "
"pomak</firstterm>, radi samo za veoma udaljene galaksije. Dakle, postoji "
"nekoliko metoda, svaka sa svojim ograničenim važnostima, a time i imenom."

#. Tag: title
#: cosmicdist.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid "Direct measurements"
msgstr "Direktna mjerenja"

#. Tag: para
#: cosmicdist.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The bottom of the ladder consists of objects whose distances can be directly "
"measured, like the moon (see <ulink url=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Lunar_Laser_Ranging_experiment\">Lunar Laser Ranging</ulink>). The same "
"technique, using radio waves, is applied to find distances to planets as "
"well."
msgstr ""
"Dno tabele se sastoji od objekata čija udaljenosti se može izravno mjeriti, "
"kao Mjesec (vidi <ulink url=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Lunar_Laser_Ranging_experiment\">Raspon lunarnog lasera</ulink>). Ista "
"tehnika, koristeći radio-talase, primjenjuje se za nalazak udaljenosti "
"planeta."

#. Tag: para
#: cosmicdist.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For nearby stars, measuring the <link linkend=\"ai-parallax\">parallax</"
"link> is possible and yields the distance to the star."
msgstr ""
"Za obližnje zvijezde, mjerenje <link linkend=\"ai-parallax\">parallax</"
"link>je moguće i daje udaljenost do zvijezda."

#. Tag: title
#: cosmicdist.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid "Standard candles"
msgstr "Standard svijeća"

#. Tag: para
#: cosmicdist.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"\"Standard candles\" are objects whose intrinsic brightnesses we can know "
"for sure. The apparent <link linkend=\"ai-magnitude\">magnitude</link>, "
"which is easy to measure, tells us how bright an object appears, not how "
"bright it actually is. Distant objects appear less brighter, because their "
"light gets spread out over a larger area."
msgstr ""
"\"Standard svijeća\" su objekti čiju unutrašnju osvetljenosti možemo znati "
"za sigurno. Prividna <link linkend=\"ai-magnitude\">veličina</link>, koju je "
"lako izmjeriti, govori nam koliko svijetao se objekat pojavljuje, a ne "
"koliko je uistinu svijetao. Udaljeni objekti izgledaju manje svjetli, jer se "
"svjetlost rasipa preko veće površine."

#. Tag: para
#: cosmicdist.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In accordance with the <firstterm>inverse square law</firstterm> for light "
"intensities, the amount of light we receive from an object drops with the "
"distance squared. Thus, we may compute the distance to an object if we know "
"both how bright it actually is (absolute magnitude; 'M') and how bright it "
"appears to us on earth (apparent magnitude; 'm'). We may define the "
"<firstterm>distance modulus</firstterm> as follows:"
msgstr ""
"U skladu sa <firstterm>zakonu obrnutog kvadrata</firstterm> za intenzitet "
"svjetlosti.  količine svetlosti dobijamo od objekta kapi sa udaljenosti na "
"kvadrat. Prema tome, možemo izračunati udaljenost do objekta ako znamo oboje "
"kako svijetle što jeste (apsolutna magnituda; 'M') i kako svijetle čini nam "
"se na Zemlji (prividne magnitude; 'm'). Mi možemo definirati<firstterm>modul "
"udaljenost </firstterm> kako slijedi:"

#. Tag: para
#: cosmicdist.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid "Distance Modulus = M - m = 5 log<subscript>10</subscript> d - 5"
msgstr "Modul udaljenosti = M - m = 5 log<subscript>10</subscript> d - 5"

#. Tag: para
#: cosmicdist.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here 'd' is the distance measured in <link linkend=\"ai-parallax\">parsecs</"
"link>."
msgstr ""
"Ovdje 'd' je udaljenost mjerena u <link linkend=\"ai-parallax\">parsecs</"
"link>."

#. Tag: para
#: cosmicdist.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For these special standard candle objects, we have some other way of knowing "
"their intrinsic brightness, and thereby can calculate their distance."
msgstr ""
"Za ovim posebnim standardnim objektima svijeća, imamo neki drugi način "
"znajući svoje unutrašnje osvjetljenje, a time se  može izračunati njihova "
"udaljenost."

#. Tag: para
#: cosmicdist.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid "Common \"standard candles\" used in astronomy are:"
msgstr "Zajednički \"standardne svijeće\" korištene u astronomiji su:"

#. Tag: para
#: cosmicdist.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Cepheid Variables: A kind of periodic variable star, whose variation period "
"is related to the luminosity"
msgstr ""
"Cepheid Variables: A vrsta periodične varijabilne zvijezde, čija se "
"varijacija perioda odnosi na sjaj"

#. Tag: para
#: cosmicdist.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"RR Lyrae Variables: Another such periodic variable star with a well-known "
"period-luminosity relationship"
msgstr ""
"RR Lyrae Variables: Još jedna takva periodične varijabla zvijezda s poznatim "
"period-sjaj odnosa"

#. Tag: para
#: cosmicdist.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Type-Ia supernovae: These supernovae have a very well-defined luminosity as "
"a result of the physics that governs them and hence serve as standard-candles"
msgstr ""
"Type-Ia supernovae: Ove supernove imaju vrlo dobro definiran sjaj kao "
"rezultat fizike koji ih uređuje i time služe kao standard-svijeće"

#. Tag: title
#: cosmicdist.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "Other methods"
msgstr "Druge metode"

#. Tag: para
#: cosmicdist.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are many other methods. Some of them rely on the physics of stars, "
"such as the relationship between luminosity and color for various types of "
"stars (this is usually represented on a <firstterm>Hertzsprung-Russel "
"Diagram</firstterm>). Some of them work for star clusters, such as the "
"<firstterm>Moving cluster method</firstterm> and the <firstterm>main-"
"sequence fitting method</firstterm>. The <firstterm>Tully-Fisher relation</"
"firstterm> that relates the brightness of a spiral galaxy to its rotation "
"can be used to find the distance modulus, since the rotation of a galaxy is "
"easy to measure using <firstterm>Doppler shift</firstterm>. Distances to "
"distant galaxies may be found by measuring the <firstterm>Cosmological "
"redshift</firstterm>, which is the redshift of light from distance galaxies "
"that results from the expansion of the universe."
msgstr ""
"Postoje mnoge druge metode. Neke od njih se oslanjaju na fizici zvijezda, "
"kao što je odnos između sjaja i boje za različite vrste zvijezda (to je "
"obično predstavljeno na <firstterm>Hertzsprung-Russel Dijagramu</"
"firstterm>). Neki od njih rade za zvijezda klastera, kao što je "
"<firstterm>Pokretne klaster metode</firstterm> i <firstterm>glavne-sekvence "
"armatura metode </firstterm>.  <firstterm>Tully-Fisher relacija</firstterm> "
"koji se odnosi osvjetljenje spirale galaksije svoje rotacije može se "
"koristiti za pronalaženje modula udaljenosti, rotaciju galaksije je lako "
"izmjeriti pomoću <firstterm>Doppler rotiranje</firstterm>. Udaljenosti do "
"udaljenih galaksija mogu se naći mjerenjem <firstterm>Kosmološki crveni "
"pomak</firstterm>, što je crveni pomak svjetla iz udaljene galaksija koji "
"proizlazi iz širenja svemira."

#. Tag: para
#: cosmicdist.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For further information, consult <ulink url=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Cosmic_distance_ladder\">Wikipedia on Cosmic Distance Ladder</ulink>"
msgstr ""
"Za više informacija, obratite se <ulink url=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Cosmic_distance_ladder\">Wikipedia Tabela kosmičkih udaljenosti</ulink>"
